{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They will graze</b> — from the root of רועה, meaning they will teach the majority of people." "<b>And lacking heart</b> — in contrast to 'righteous.'" "<b>And fools</b> — in contrast to 'many,' meaning and fools, on account of a man lacking heart, will go astray." "<b>Will die</b> — before the time of fullness."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:55.324968475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}